WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.890
In the western Scottish mountains, over
4,000 millimetres of rain falls in a year.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.870
In the driest parts of eastern
England, it's around 500.

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.210
Same island.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.410
About eight times the rain.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.370
So what makes one side of Britain
so much wetter than the other?

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.310
In this mission, you'll
separate weather from climate,

7
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.570
and map the UK's
temperatures and rainfall.

8
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.650
Then you'll trace what
controls the UK's climate,

9
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.150
starting with how far north a place is.

10
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.390
Your mission: find out why the west of
Scotland is so much wetter than the east

11
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.320
of England.
